{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>You shall surely open your hand.</b> Even a hundred times. <br><b>And you shall surely lend him.</b> If he did not want a gift, give to him by way of a loan. <br><b>Sufficient for his need.</b> And you are not commanded to make him wealthy. <br><b>Which he lacks.</b> Even a horse to ride upon and a servant to run before him. <br><b>To him.</b> Even to marry him a wife, from what is written (Genesis 2:18): ״אעשה לו עזר כנגדו״."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:48:22.712474297Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}